/-!
# The strict transform on an affine chart is the ring-level strict transform

[Stacks, Tag 0810] is a statement about rings: for `R → S` flat of finite presentation with
geometrically integral fibres and `M` a finite `S`-module, it produces a finitely generated ideal
`I ⊆ R` such that on every affine blowup chart `R' = R[I/a]` the quotient of `S' ⊗_S M` by its
`a`-power torsion, `S' = S ⊗_R R'`, is free of finite rank near every point of `Spec R'`. What
makes it a statement about the *strict transform* of [Stacks, Tag 080D] is the identification
proved here: on an affine chart of the base change over which the inverse image of the centre is
generated by a single element `β`, the strict transform of a quasi-coherent module is the module
attached to the quotient of the chart-level base change by its `β`-power torsion.

That identification is what [Stacks, Tag 0811] consumes: it is the only step of its proof which
relates the geometric construction to the affine engine, and nothing in the library supplied it.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.pullbackTildeIsoOfAffineIso`: the pullback of a quasi-coherent module on an
  affine scheme along a morphism from an affine scheme is the extension of scalars of its module
  of global sections. This is [Stacks, Tag 01I9] with the two affine identifications inserted.
* `Stacks.StrictTransform.affineChartSheafIso`: **the strict transform on an affine chart.**
* `Stacks.StrictTransform.affineChartSheafBlowUpIso`: the same along a blowup, with no hypothesis
  on the centre.

## Implementation notes

The three steps are independent. `Stacks.StrictTransform.pullbackSheafIso` carries the strict
transform onto the chart, as the quotient of the pullback of `F` there by the sections supported on
the preimage of the exceptional preimage. The hypothesis `hZ` says that preimage is the zero locus
of `β`, so `AlgebraicGeometry.tildeSupportedQuotientZeroLocusIso` computes the quotient as the
`β`-power torsion quotient. In between, the ambient module has to be recognized as a `tilde`: that
is `AlgebraicGeometry.pullbackTildeIsoOfAffineIso`, transported across the quotient by
`Stacks.SupportedQuotient.supportedSectionsCokernelIso`.

The chart is given as an arbitrary open immersion `j : Spec B ⟶ X ×_S S'` together with the ring
map `ρ` it induces on `X`, rather than as a blowup chart: that is strictly more general, needs no
bookkeeping about the two realizations of the affine blowup algebra `R[I/a]`, and is what the
covering statement `Stacks.Blowup.iSup_opensRange_blowUpAffineChart` ([Stacks, Tag 0804]) produces
one of for each `a` in the centre.

`AlgebraicGeometry.principalZeroLocus` is the zero locus of the principal ideal generated by the
image of `β` under `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.ΓSpecIso`, which is the form the supported-sections
machinery works in; the ring-level statements of [Stacks, Tag 07Z3]
(`Stacks.Blowup.affineBlowup_idealMap_eq_span`) deliver exactly the generator `β`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0810](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0810)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 080D](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/080D)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0804](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0804)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01I9](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01I9)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07Z3](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07Z3)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory Limits AlgebraicGeometry Opposite TopologicalSpace
open AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules
open scoped TensorProduct

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- **The pullback of a quasi-coherent module on an affine scheme to an affine scheme.** Let `X`
be affine, let `F` be presented as `M^~` through `X ≅ Spec Γ(X, ⊤)`, and let `g : Spec B ⟶ X` be
a morphism inducing `ρ : Γ(X, ⊤) ⟶ B`. Then `g^* F` is the module attached to `B ⊗_{Γ(X,⊤)} M`.

This is [Stacks, Tag 01I9], `AlgebraicGeometry.pullbackTildeIso`, composed with the presentation
of `F` and the identification of `g` with `Spec ρ`. -/
public def pullbackTildeIsoOfAffineIso {X : Scheme.{u}} [IsAffine X] (F : X.Modules)
    (M : ModuleCat.{u} Γ(X, ⊤)) (e : F ≅ (Scheme.Modules.pullback X.isoSpec.hom).obj (tilde M))
    (B : CommRingCat.{u}) (g : Spec B ⟶ X) (ρ : Γ(X, ⊤) ⟶ B)
    (hg : g ≫ X.isoSpec.hom = Spec.map ρ) :
    (Scheme.Modules.pullback g).obj F ≅ tilde ((ModuleCat.extendScalars ρ.hom).obj M) :=
  (Scheme.Modules.pullback g).mapIso e ≪≫
    (Scheme.Modules.pullbackComp g X.isoSpec.hom).app (tilde M) ≪≫
    (Scheme.Modules.pullbackCongr hg).app (tilde M) ≪≫
    (pullbackTildeIso Γ(X, ⊤) B ρ).app M

end AlgebraicGeometry

namespace Stacks.StrictTransform

variable {X S S' : Scheme.{u}}

/-- **The strict transform on an affine chart is the `β`-power torsion quotient of the chart-level
base change.** Let `X` be affine with a quasi-coherent module `F` presented as `M^~`, let
`b : S' ⟶ S` be a second morphism and `E` an ideal sheaf on `S'` whose support has affine open
complement, and let `j : Spec B ⟶ X ×_S S'` be an affine chart of the base change, inducing
`ρ : Γ(X, ⊤) ⟶ B` on `X`. If the inverse image under `j` of `pr_{S'}^{-1}(Supp E)` is the zero
locus of `β : B`, then the strict transform of `F` pulled back to the chart is the module attached
to

  `(B ⊗_{Γ(X,⊤)} M) / (β`-power torsion`)`.

This is the geometric form of the module produced by the affine engine [Stacks, Tag 0810]: on a
blowup chart `R[I/a]` the inverse image of the centre is generated by the image of `a`
([Stacks, Tag 07Z3]), so `β` is that image and the right-hand side is literally the module
`exists_fg_ideal_forall_blowup_chart_exists_away_basis` produces a basis for. -/
public def affineChartSheafIso [IsAffine X] (f : X ⟶ S) (b : S' ⟶ S) (E : S'.IdealSheafData)
    [IsAffineHom (Scheme.Opens.ι E.support.compl)] (F : X.Modules) [F.IsQuasicoherent]
    (M : ModuleCat.{u} Γ(X, ⊤)) (e : F ≅ (Scheme.Modules.pullback X.isoSpec.hom).obj (tilde M))
    (B : CommRingCat.{u}) (j : Spec B ⟶ baseChange f b) [IsOpenImmersion j]
    (ρ : Γ(X, ⊤) ⟶ B) (β : B)
    (hfst : (j ≫ pullback.fst f b) ≫ X.isoSpec.hom = Spec.map ρ)
    (hZ : j.base ⁻¹' exceptionalPreimage f b E = principalZeroLocus B β) :
    (Scheme.Modules.pullback j).obj (sheaf f b E F) ≅
      tilde (ModuleCat.of B (((ModuleCat.extendScalars ρ.hom).obj M) ⧸
        Submodule.torsion' B ((ModuleCat.extendScalars ρ.hom).obj M)
          (Submonoid.powers β))) := by
  refine pullbackSheafIso f b E F j ≪≫ ?_
  rw [hZ]
  exact Stacks.SupportedQuotient.supportedSectionsCokernelIso _
      (pullbackTildeIsoOfAffineIso F M e B (j ≫ pullback.fst f b) ρ hfst) ≪≫
    tildeSupportedQuotientZeroLocusIso ((ModuleCat.extendScalars ρ.hom).obj M) β

/-- **The strict transform along a blowup, on an affine chart.** The instance of
`Stacks.StrictTransform.affineChartSheafIso` at `b` the blowup of `S` in `I` and `E` its
exceptional ideal, where the affineness hypothesis is automatic. -/
public def affineChartSheafBlowUpIso [IsAffine X] (f : X ⟶ S) (I : S.IdealSheafData)
    (F : X.Modules) [F.IsQuasicoherent] (M : ModuleCat.{u} Γ(X, ⊤))
    (e : F ≅ (Scheme.Modules.pullback X.isoSpec.hom).obj (tilde M)) (B : CommRingCat.{u})
    (j : Spec B ⟶ baseChange f (blowUpToBase I)) [IsOpenImmersion j] (ρ : Γ(X, ⊤) ⟶ B) (β : B)
    (hfst : (j ≫ pullback.fst f (blowUpToBase I)) ≫ X.isoSpec.hom = Spec.map ρ)
    (hZ : j.base ⁻¹' exceptionalPreimage f (blowUpToBase I) (exceptionalIdeal I) =
      principalZeroLocus B β) :
    (Scheme.Modules.pullback j).obj (sheaf f (blowUpToBase I) (exceptionalIdeal I) F) ≅
      tilde (ModuleCat.of B (((ModuleCat.extendScalars ρ.hom).obj M) ⧸
        Submodule.torsion' B ((ModuleCat.extendScalars ρ.hom).obj M)
          (Submonoid.powers β))) :=
  have : IsAffineHom (Scheme.Opens.ι (exceptionalIdeal I).support.compl) :=
    Stacks.Divisors.isAffineHom_compl_of_isEffectiveCartierDivisor _
      (Stacks.Blowup.isEffectiveCartierDivisor_exceptionalIdeal I)
  affineChartSheafIso f (blowUpToBase I) (exceptionalIdeal I) F M e B j ρ β hfst hZ

/-- **The conclusion of [Stacks, Tag 0810], geometrized.** In the situation of
`Stacks.StrictTransform.affineChartSheafIso`, if the chart-level strict transform becomes free of
rank `r` after inverting `g : B`, then the strict transform itself, pulled back to the chart, is
free of rank `r` on the basic open of `g`.

The hypothesis is verbatim the conclusion of
`exists_fg_ideal_forall_blowup_chart_exists_away_basis` ([Stacks, Tag 0810]) at one prime of the
chart base: that statement produces, for each prime `p'` of `R'`, an element `g` of `S'` outside
`p'S'` after inverting which the `a`-power torsion quotient of `S' ⊗_S M` is free of rank `r`.
This turns that algebra into local freeness of the strict transform of [Stacks, Tag 080D], which
is the form [Stacks, Tag 0811] consumes. -/
public theorem nonempty_restrict_basicOpen_free_of_basis [IsAffine X] (f : X ⟶ S) (b : S' ⟶ S)
    (E : S'.IdealSheafData) [IsAffineHom (Scheme.Opens.ι E.support.compl)] (F : X.Modules)
    [F.IsQuasicoherent] (M : ModuleCat.{u} Γ(X, ⊤))
    (e : F ≅ (Scheme.Modules.pullback X.isoSpec.hom).obj (tilde M)) (B : CommRingCat.{u})
    (j : Spec B ⟶ baseChange f b) [IsOpenImmersion j] (ρ : Γ(X, ⊤) ⟶ B) (β : B)
    (hfst : (j ≫ pullback.fst f b) ≫ X.isoSpec.hom = Spec.map ρ)
    (hZ : j.base ⁻¹' exceptionalPreimage f b E = principalZeroLocus B β) (g : B) (r : ℕ)
    (hbasis : Nonempty (Module.Basis (Fin r) (Localization.Away g)
      (LocalizedModule (Submonoid.powers g)
        (((ModuleCat.extendScalars ρ.hom).obj M) ⧸
          Submodule.torsion' B ((ModuleCat.extendScalars ρ.hom).obj M)
            (Submonoid.powers β))))) :
    Nonempty (((Scheme.Modules.pullback j).obj (sheaf f b E F)).restrict
      (specBasicOpen B g).ι ≅ SheafOfModules.free.{u} (ULift.{u} (Fin r))) :=
  ⟨(Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctor (specBasicOpen B g).ι).mapIso
      (affineChartSheafIso f b E F M e B j ρ β hfst hZ) ≪≫
    ((tilde_restrict_basicOpen_rank_iff B _ g r).mpr hbasis).some⟩

/-! ### Tag 0810 on a scheme -/

/-- **Base change of a module along the structure map of an algebra, in its two spellings.** The
extension of scalars of `ModuleCat` along a ring map `φ : A →+* B` and the tensor product
`B ⊗[A] M` over an algebra structure whose structure map is `φ` are the same tensor product,
formed over two `A`-module structures on `B`: the first over `Module.compHom B φ`, the second
over `Algebra.toModule`. The two agree, because an algebra structure is determined by its
structure map (`Algebra.algebra_ext`) and `RingHom.toAlgebra` is the one whose scalar
multiplication is literally `φ c * x`.

This is the only discrepancy between the module the ring-level [Stacks, Tag 0810] produces a
basis for and the one `Stacks.StrictTransform.affineChartSheafIso` computes the strict transform
on a chart to be. -/
public noncomputable def extendScalarsAlgebraMapEquiv {A B : Type u} [CommRing A] [CommRing B]
    (φ : A →+* B) [inst : Algebra A B] (hφ : (algebraMap A B : A →+* B) = φ)
    (M : ModuleCat.{u} A) :
    (ModuleCat.extendScalars φ).obj M ≃ₗ[B] B ⊗[A] M := by
  have h : φ.toAlgebra = inst := hφ ▸ toAlgebra_algebraMap
  rw [← h]
  exact LinearEquiv.refl B _

/-- **The away-basis conclusion of the ring-level [Stacks, Tag 0810], in the spelling the chart
identification consumes.** The ring-level statement produces a linear equivalence of the
localization of the chart-level torsion quotient of `B ⊗[A] M` with a finite free module;
`Stacks.StrictTransform.nonempty_restrict_basicOpen_free_of_basis` asks for a basis of the same
localization with `B ⊗[A] M` written as the `ModuleCat` extension of scalars along the structure
map. `Stacks.StrictTransform.extendScalarsAlgebraMapEquiv` identifies the two modules,
`Stacks.quotientTorsionPowersEquiv` carries that across the torsion quotient,
`IsLocalizedModule.mapEquiv` across the localization, and `Module.Basis.ofEquivFun` turns the
resulting equivalence with `Fin r → Localization.Away g` into a basis. -/
public theorem nonempty_basis_extendScalars_quotient {A B : Type u} [CommRing A] [CommRing B]
    [Algebra A B] (φ : A →+* B) (hφ : (algebraMap A B : A →+* B) = φ) (M : ModuleCat.{u} A)
    (β g : B) (r : ℕ)
    (h : Nonempty (LocalizedModule (Submonoid.powers g)
        ((B ⊗[A] M) ⧸ Submodule.torsion' B (B ⊗[A] M) (Submonoid.powers β)) ≃ₗ[Localization.Away g]
      (Fin r → Localization.Away g))) :
    Nonempty (Module.Basis (Fin r) (Localization.Away g)
      (LocalizedModule (Submonoid.powers g)
        (((ModuleCat.extendScalars φ).obj M) ⧸
          Submodule.torsion' B ((ModuleCat.extendScalars φ).obj M) (Submonoid.powers β)))) := by
  obtain ⟨ψ⟩ := h
  exact ⟨Module.Basis.ofEquivFun (LinearEquiv.trans
    (IsLocalizedModule.mapEquiv (Submonoid.powers g)
      (LocalizedModule.mkLinearMap (Submonoid.powers g) _)
      (LocalizedModule.mkLinearMap (Submonoid.powers g) _) (Localization.Away g)
      (Stacks.quotientTorsionPowersEquiv β (extendScalarsAlgebraMapEquiv φ hφ M))) ψ)⟩

/-- **The conclusion of [Stacks, Tag 0810] on one affine chart of a base change.** Let `X` be
affine with a quasi-coherent module `F`, let `B` be a ring with a map
`ρ : Γ(X, ⊤) ⟶ B`, let `β : B`, let `r : ℕ` and let `J ⊆ B` be an ideal. This says: for every
second morphism `b : Y ⟶ S`, every ideal sheaf `E` on `Y` whose support has affine open
complement, and every open immersion `j : Spec B ⟶ X ×_S Y` inducing `ρ` on `X` and carrying
`pr_Y^{-1}(Supp E)` to the zero locus of `β`, the strict transform of `F` of
[Stacks, Tag 080D], pulled back to the chart, is free of rank `r` on the basic open of some
`g : B` outside `J`.

This is the geometric form of one instance of the conclusion of [Stacks, Tag 0810]: there `B` is
the chart algebra `S ⊗_R R[I/a]`, `β` the image of `a`, and `J` the extension `p'S'` of a prime
of `R[I/a]`. -/
public def ChartFreeOfRank [IsAffine X] (f : X ⟶ S) (F : X.Modules) [F.IsQuasicoherent]
    (B : CommRingCat.{u}) (ρ : Γ(X, ⊤) ⟶ B) (β : B) (r : ℕ) (J : Ideal B) : Prop :=
  ∀ {Y : Scheme.{u}} (b : Y ⟶ S) (E : Y.IdealSheafData)
    [IsAffineHom (Scheme.Opens.ι E.support.compl)] (j : Spec B ⟶ baseChange f b)
    [IsOpenImmersion j],
    (j ≫ pullback.fst f b) ≫ X.isoSpec.hom = Spec.map ρ →
    j.base ⁻¹' exceptionalPreimage f b E = principalZeroLocus B β →
    ∃ g : B, g ∉ J ∧
      Nonempty (((Scheme.Modules.pullback j).obj (sheaf f b E F)).restrict
        (specBasicOpen B g).ι ≅ SheafOfModules.free.{u} (ULift.{u} (Fin r)))

/-- **The away-basis conclusion of the ring-level [Stacks, Tag 0810] gives
`Stacks.StrictTransform.ChartFreeOfRank`.** On a chart with structure map `algebraMap Γ(X, ⊤) B`,
an element `g ∉ J` after inverting which the `β`-power torsion quotient of `B ⊗_{Γ(X,⊤)} M`
becomes free of rank `r` makes the strict transform free of rank `r` on `D(g)`.

The two steps are `Stacks.StrictTransform.nonempty_basis_extendScalars_quotient`, which puts the
ring-level equivalence in the spelling the chart identification consumes, and
`Stacks.StrictTransform.nonempty_restrict_basicOpen_free_of_basis`, which is that
identification. -/
public theorem chartFreeOfRank_of_nonempty_equiv [IsAffine X] (f : X ⟶ S) (F : X.Modules)
    [F.IsQuasicoherent] (M : ModuleCat.{u} Γ(X, ⊤))
    (e : F ≅ (Scheme.Modules.pullback X.isoSpec.hom).obj (tilde M))
    (B : Type u) [CommRing B] [Algebra Γ(X, ⊤) B] (β : B) (r : ℕ) (J : Ideal B) (g : B)
    (hg : g ∉ J)
    (h : Nonempty (LocalizedModule (Submonoid.powers g)
        ((B ⊗[Γ(X, ⊤)] M) ⧸ Submodule.torsion' B (B ⊗[Γ(X, ⊤)] M) (Submonoid.powers β))
      ≃ₗ[Localization.Away g] (Fin r → Localization.Away g))) :
    ChartFreeOfRank f F (CommRingCat.of B)
      (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap Γ(X, ⊤) B)) β r J := by
  intro Y b E _ j _ hfst hZ
  exact ⟨g, hg,
    nonempty_restrict_basicOpen_free_of_basis f b E F M e (CommRingCat.of B) j
      (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap Γ(X, ⊤) B)) β hfst hZ g r
      (nonempty_basis_extendScalars_quotient (algebraMap Γ(X, ⊤) B) rfl M β g r h)⟩

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0810, read on the strict transform.** Let `S` be an affine scheme, `X`
an affine scheme over it with `Γ(S, ⊤) ⟶ Γ(X, ⊤)` flat and of finite presentation with
geometrically integral fibres, let `F` be a quasi-coherent module on `X` presented as `M^~` with
`M` finite over `Γ(X, ⊤)`, let `t : Γ(S, ⊤)` and `r : ℕ`, and assume `M` is finitely presented
after inverting `t` and free of rank `r` at every extended prime `qΓ(X, ⊤)` with `t ∉ q`. Then
there is a finitely generated ideal `I ⊆ Γ(S, ⊤)` with `V(t) = V(I)` such that for every `a ∈ I`
and every prime `q'` of the affine blowup algebra `Γ(S, ⊤)[I/a]`, the chart
`Spec (Γ(X, ⊤) ⊗_{Γ(S,⊤)} Γ(S, ⊤)[I/a])` of a base change satisfies
`Stacks.StrictTransform.ChartFreeOfRank` for the image of `a` and the extension of `q'`: on every
such chart on which the inverse image of the centre is the zero locus of the image of `a`, the
strict transform of `F` of [Stacks, Tag 080D] is free of rank `r` on a basic open `D(g)` with `g`
outside `q'·(Γ(X, ⊤) ⊗ Γ(S, ⊤)[I/a])`.

This is the scheme-level form of the ring-level
`exists_fg_ideal_forall_blowup_chart_exists_away_basis`: the ideal, the chart algebras and the
element `g` are the ring-level ones, and the module the ring-level statement produces a basis for
is identified with the strict transform by `Stacks.StrictTransform.affineChartSheafIso`, through
`Stacks.StrictTransform.nonempty_restrict_basicOpen_free_of_basis`. It is the form the proof of
[Stacks, Tag 0811] consumes, which is about the strict transform and not about the chart-level
torsion quotient: freeness of the strict transform near the generic point of a fibre of
`X ×_S Bl_I(S) ⟶ Bl_I(S)` is the flatness conjunct of
`AlgebraicGeometry.GenericFibreFlatteningBlowup`.

The charts are universally quantified inside `Stacks.StrictTransform.ChartFreeOfRank`: nothing is
claimed here about their existence, which is the content of [Stacks, Tag 0804] for the blowup of
`S` in `I` together with the base change of that covering along `f`. -/
@[stacks 0810 "the conclusion read on the strict transform of [Stacks, Tag 080D]: on every \
affine chart of a base change on which the inverse image of the centre is the zero locus of the \
image of the chart's denominator, the strict transform of the module is free of rank r on a \
basic open through every extended prime of the chart base. The hypotheses are the source's own, \
read on the global sections of the two affine schemes; the existence of such charts is not \
claimed"]
public theorem exists_fg_ideal_forall_chartFreeOfRank [IsAffine X] [IsAffine S] (f : X ⟶ S)
    (F : X.Modules) [F.IsQuasicoherent] (M : ModuleCat.{u} Γ(X, ⊤))
    (e : F ≅ (Scheme.Modules.pullback X.isoSpec.hom).obj (tilde M))
    [Algebra Γ(S, ⊤) Γ(X, ⊤)]
    (halg : (algebraMap Γ(S, ⊤) Γ(X, ⊤) : Γ(S, ⊤) →+* Γ(X, ⊤)) = f.appTop.hom)
    [Algebra.FinitePresentation Γ(S, ⊤) Γ(X, ⊤)] [Module.Flat Γ(S, ⊤) Γ(X, ⊤)]
    [Module.Finite Γ(X, ⊤) M] (t : Γ(S, ⊤)) (r : ℕ)
    (hfibre : ∀ (q : Ideal Γ(S, ⊤)) (hq : q.IsPrime),
      letI := hq
      Algebra.IsGeometricallyIntegral q.ResidueField (q.Fiber Γ(X, ⊤)))
    (hfp : Module.FinitePresentation (Localization.Away (algebraMap Γ(S, ⊤) Γ(X, ⊤) t))
      (LocalizedModule (Submonoid.powers (algebraMap Γ(S, ⊤) Γ(X, ⊤) t)) M))
    (hrank : ∀ (q : Ideal Γ(S, ⊤)) (hq : q.IsPrime), t ∉ q →
      letI := hq
      let 𝔮 := Ideal.map (algebraMap Γ(S, ⊤) Γ(X, ⊤)) q
      ∀ h𝔮 : 𝔮.IsPrime,
        letI := h𝔮
        Nonempty (LocalizedModule 𝔮.primeCompl M ≃ₗ[Localization 𝔮.primeCompl]
          (Fin r → Localization 𝔮.primeCompl))) :
    ∃ I : Ideal Γ(S, ⊤), I.FG ∧
      (∀ q : Ideal Γ(S, ⊤), q.IsPrime → (t ∈ q ↔ I ≤ q)) ∧
      ∀ (a : Γ(S, ⊤)) (ha : a ∈ I),
        letI : Fact (a ∈ I) := ⟨ha⟩
        ∀ q' : Ideal (Blowup I a), q'.IsPrime →
          ChartFreeOfRank f F (CommRingCat.of (Γ(X, ⊤) ⊗[Γ(S, ⊤)] Blowup I a))
            (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap Γ(X, ⊤) (Γ(X, ⊤) ⊗[Γ(S, ⊤)] Blowup I a)))
            (algebraMap Γ(X, ⊤) (Γ(X, ⊤) ⊗[Γ(S, ⊤)] Blowup I a) (f.appTop.hom a)) r
            (Ideal.map Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight q') := by
  let : Module Γ(S, ⊤) M := Module.compHom M (algebraMap Γ(S, ⊤) Γ(X, ⊤))
  have : IsScalarTower Γ(S, ⊤) Γ(X, ⊤) M :=
    ⟨fun x y z ↦ by rw [Algebra.smul_def]; exact mul_smul _ _ _⟩
  obtain ⟨I, hIfg, hIsupp, hchart⟩ :=
    exists_fg_ideal_forall_blowup_chart_exists_away_basis Γ(S, ⊤) Γ(X, ⊤) M t r hfibre hfp hrank
  refine ⟨I, hIfg, hIsupp, ?_⟩
  intro a ha
  let : Fact (a ∈ I) := ⟨ha⟩
  intro q' hq'
  obtain ⟨g, hg, hbasis⟩ := hchart a ha q' hq'
  rw [← halg]
  exact chartFreeOfRank_of_nonempty_equiv f F M e (Γ(X, ⊤) ⊗[Γ(S, ⊤)] Blowup I a) _ r _ g hg
    hbasis

end Stacks.StrictTransform

end
